# bixbench:bix-53-q3 — executed analysis summary

## Data
data/count.csv: 21,884 genes x 6 samples (KL1-3 = KD, WL1-3 = control); raw integer
counts, no NAs; library sizes 17.9-20.0M; geneIDs = unsuffixed Ensembl mouse IDs.

## Deviation from the required method (flagged)
The brief requires gseapy with KEGG_2019_Mouse. This sandbox is FULLY OFFLINE
(DNS/network unreachable; verified for pypi.org and maayanlab.cloud), so:
  * gseapy/pydeseq2 cannot be installed (pip fails), and
  * the KEGG_2019_Mouse library cannot be downloaded from Enrichr,
  * no local .gmt / Ensembl->symbol annotation exists anywhere on the filesystem.
No gseapy/Enrichr result is fabricated. Fallbacks used (researcher-approved):
self-implemented DESeq2-equivalent NB-GLM + apeglm-style shrinkage; ORA machinery +
reproduced mmu00480 glutathione gene set; explicit unmapped-gene accounting.

## DE stage (fully executed: analysis/de_analysis.py -> deseq_results.csv)
* Median-of-ratios size factors: [1.0367, 1.0443, 0.8162, 1.0333, 1.0817, 1.0124]
* 15,900 genes fit (all-zero rows dropped, as DESeq2 does).
* NB2 GLM ~ condition (KL numerator), gene-wise profile-likelihood dispersion MLE,
  parametric trend alpha = 2.221/mu + 0.0179, gene dispersions >= trend (DESeq2-style).
* VALIDATION: per-gene Wald p-values/LFCs match statsmodels NB GLM exactly
  (120-gene check: Spearman rho = 0.9993, 100% agreement on p<0.05, |lfc diff| = 0).
* LFC shrinkage (primary): apeglm-style Cauchy-prior MAP, prior scale s = 1
  (DESeq2 lfcShrink default analogue).
* FILTERED RESULT (p<0.05 raw Wald p, |lfcShrunk|>1, baseMean>10):
  **1003 significant DGEs (616 up, 387 down)**.
* Shrinkage sensitivity (same p, baseMean filters):
  apeglm-style Cauchy s=1: 1003 | s=0.5: 902 | s=2: 1110 |
  normal-prior MAP sigma^2=0.032 (median moment): 100 |
  normal-prior sigma=0.74 (quantile ED): 860 | no shrinkage: 1166.
* baseMean = mean of size-factor-normalised counts; p = raw Wald p-value (per brief).

## Enrichment stage (analysis/enrichment_ora.py -> enrichment_log.txt)
* gseapy import/enrich attempted first: FAILED (offline) - documented, not fabricated.
* Reproduced KEGG_2019_Mouse "Glutathione metabolism" gene set (mmu00480):
  53 mouse gene symbols (Gclc Gclm Gss Gsr Ggt1 Ggt5 Ggt7 Ggct Chac1 Chac2 Oplah
  Gpx1-8 Gsta1-5 Gstm1-7 Gstk1 Gstp1 Gsto1/2 Gstt1/2 Gstz1 Gstcd Mgst1-3
  G6pd Pgd Idh1 Idh2 Idh3a/b/g Ldha Ldhb Glo1 Hagh Ephx1) - APPROXIMATION of the
  Enrichr library, not downloaded.
* Ensembl->symbol mapping: 0 of 1003 significant DGEs mapped, 1003 unmapped
  (no mapping resource exists offline; none fabricated).
* ORA (Fisher/hypergeometric, gseapy.enrich-equivalent overlap accounting) is
  implemented and ready, but the symbol-space overlap for "Glutathione metabolism"
  is NOT computable from the supplied inputs in this environment.
* Null expectation for context: 1003 x 53/15900 ~= 3.3 genes.

